p.src:
Begin with the pre-Einstein relation between a frame at rest and a train moving at velocity $v$ along the $x$-axis: $\begin{aligned}
x' &= x-vt, & t'&=t.
\end{aligned}$ The second equation contains Newton’s assumption of universal time. Every observer uses the same simultaneity slices, even though the spatial origins move relative to one another.

