p.src:
Let each half of the trip take coordinate time $T$ in the home frame. The home twin’s proper time is $\tau_{\mathrm{home}}=2T.$ The turn-around event has coordinates $(vT,T)$. The first traveling leg therefore contributes $\begin{aligned}
\tau_{\mathrm{leg}}
&=\sqrt{T^2-v^2T^2}
=T\sqrt{1-v^2}.\end{aligned}$ The return leg contributes the same amount, hence $\tau_{\mathrm{travel}}=2T\sqrt{1-v^2}<2T.$

