p.src:
The selected endpoint separation is spacelike, so use the positive spatial form of the invariant: $x'^2-t'^2=x^2-t^2.$ At the chosen endpoint, $t'=0$, $x=1$, and $t=v$. Hence $\begin{aligned}
x'^2&=1-v^2,\\
x'&=\sqrt{1-v^2}.\end{aligned}$ Thus a rest length $L$ is measured in the moving frame as $L'=L\sqrt{1-v^2/c^2}=\frac{L}{\gamma}.$

